10 REM ==========================================================
11 REM BASIC++ PROGRESSIVE TEST SUITE - I/O & DISPLAY
12 REM ==========================================================
13 REM GOAL: 
14 REM To validate and verify that the Input/Output, Display, Audio, 
15 REM Hardware, and Keyboard keywords are 100% bug-free and behave
16 REM according to the ECMA-116 and GW-BASIC standards.
17 REM 
18 REM WHAT WE ARE TESTING FOR:
19 REM - Input / Output: CLS, COLOR, CONSOLE, HOME, IMAGE, INKEY, INKEY$, INPUT, INPUT$, LINE, LOCATE, PRINT, WIDTH, WRITE, ONKEY$, USING
20 REM - Display/Screen: GRAPHICS, SCREEN, VIEW, WINDOW, TAB, SPC, CSRLIN, POS
21 REM - Audio: BEEP, SOUND, PLAY
22 REM - Hardware/Ports: INP, OUT, WAIT
23 REM - Keyboard/Macros: KEY
24 REM - Printer: LPRINT, LLIST
25 REM 
26 REM EXPECTATIONS:
27 REM - CLS should clear the screen and reset cursor to 1,1.
28 REM - PRINT USING should correctly format strings and numbers.
29 REM - INPUT / LINE INPUT / INPUT$ should handle data from the buffer if provided.
30 REM - INP/OUT should safely stub or execute depending on hardware configuration.
31 REM - BEEP / SOUND / PLAY should successfully parse and execute (or stub silently on Linux without ALSA).
32 REM - Any syntax parsing failure or unexpected execution state will trigger an ERROR.
33 REM 
34 REM HOW IT SHOULD WORK:
35 REM It executes a series of isolated subroutines, each testing an I/O structure.
36 REM If a condition fails, it calls `ERROR <ErrorCode>` which halts execution with HOW?.
37 REM 
38 REM WHERE TO MAKE CHANGES IN C SOURCE:
39 REM - `source/io/parser_io.c`: PRINT, INPUT, WRITE, LPRINT, LLIST
40 REM - `source/display/parser_display.c`: CLS, HOME, LOCATE, WIDTH, INK, PAPER, BORDER
41 REM - `source/graphics/parser_graphics.c`: GRAPHICS, SCREEN, COLOR, VIEW, WINDOW, LINE
42 REM - `source/audio/parser_audio.c`: BEEP, SOUND, PLAY
43 REM - `source/misc/parser_misc.c`: IMAGE, INP, OUT, WAIT, KEY
44 REM - `source/core/eval.c`: INKEY$, INPUT$, CSRLIN, POS, TAB, SPC
45 REM 
46 REM WHAT CAN BE CHANGED IN C SOURCE:
47 REM - The parser AST generation and runtime evaluation logic.
48 REM 
49 REM WHAT CANNOT BE CHANGED IN C SOURCE:
50 REM - Do not remove or disable standard error bounds checking.
51 REM - Do not rely on OS-specific I/O directly in parser; use `console.h` or `gw_sdl2.h`.
52 REM 
53 REM WHAT TO EXPECT:
54 REM - This suite runs entirely automatically. It avoids blocking on INPUT by relying on direct checks or file mapping if needed, but primarily tests parsing and basic execution states.
55 REM 
56 REM WHAT TO DO IF SOMETHING BREAKS:
57 REM - Check `CHANGELOG.txt` to see if a recent change to AST or Virtual Devices altered I/O flow.
58 REM - Run with `--debug` and `--log` to view the AST and execution trace.
59 REM ==========================================================
100 GOSUB 1000 : REM Test Display & Screen 
110 GOSUB 2000 : REM Test Print & Write & Using
120 GOSUB 3000 : REM Test Hardware & Audio
130 GOSUB 4000 : REM Test Keyboard & Input Modifiers
999 PRINT "ALL I/O TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY" : END
1000 REM === Display & Screen ===
1010 CLS
1020 HOME
1030 LOCATE 5, 10
1040 IF CSRLIN <> 5 THEN ERROR 50
1050 IF POS(0) <> 10 THEN ERROR 51
1060 WIDTH 80
1070 COLOR 14, 1
1080 CONSOLE
1090 SCREEN 0
1100 GRAPHICS 0
1110 VIEW PRINT 1 TO 24
1120 WINDOW (0,0)-(100,100)
1125 LINE (0,0)-(50,50), 1, B
1130 RETURN
2000 REM === Print & Write & Using ===
2010 PRINT "HELLO"; SPC(5); "WORLD"
2020 PRINT TAB(15); "BASIC++"
2030 WRITE "DATA", 123
2040 REM (Removed variable assignment for A$)
2050 PRINT USING "###.##"; 12.345
2055 IMAGE "###.##"
2060 LPRINT "TESTING PRINTER"
2065 LLIST
2070 OPEN "test_input.txt" FOR OUTPUT AS #1
2075 PRINT #1, "HELLO", 42
2080 PRINT #1, "LINE 2 DATA"
2085 CLOSE #1
2090 OPEN "test_input.txt" FOR INPUT AS #1
2095 INPUT #1, IN1$, IN2
2100 LINE INPUT #1, IN3$
2105 CLOSE #1
2110 IF IN1$ <> "HELLO" THEN ERROR 52
2115 IF IN2 <> 42 THEN ERROR 53
2120 IF IN3$ <> "LINE 2 DATA" THEN ERROR 54
2125 OPEN "test_input.txt" FOR INPUT AS #1
2130 I$ = INPUT$(5, 1)
2135 CLOSE #1
2140 IF I$ <> "HELLO" THEN ERROR 55
2150 RETURN
3000 REM === Hardware & Audio ===
3010 BEEP
3020 SOUND 440, 10
3030 PLAY "O4 C D E F G"
3040 OUT &H378, 255
3050 V = INP(&H378)
3055 WAIT &H378, 1, 1
3060 RETURN
4000 REM === Keyboard & Input Modifiers ===
4010 REM (INKEY$ and INKEY removed from automated tests because they block)
4020 KEY 1, "MENU" + CHR$(13)
4030 O$ = ONKEY$
4040 ON KEY(1) GOSUB 4100
4050 RETURN
